#: ../../source/docs/common-erle-brain-linux-autopilot.rst:255
#: e2d703feb32e4c9382ebb60d4f8dd594
msgid ""
"Erle-Brain comes with full support for `Snappy Ubuntu Core "
"<http://www.ubuntu.com/internet-of-things>`__. Just fetch one of the "
"`available images "
"<http://erlerobotics.com/docs/Artificial_Brains_and_Autopilots/Operating_System_images/Ubuntu.html>`__"
" (for the microSD card) and start developing *snaps*."
msgstr ""
"Erle-Brain 完整支持 `Snappy Ubuntu Core <http://www.ubuntu.com/internet-of-"
"things>`__。只需获取其中一个 `可用镜像 "
"<http://erlerobotics.com/docs/Artificial_Brains_and_Autopilots/Operating_System_images/Ubuntu.html>`__"
" （用于 microSD 卡）并开始开发 *snap* 应用。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-erle-brain-linux-autopilot.rst:260
#: d02ffe4c1b2845ec9e8d035bb6e5dacc
msgid ""
"Snappy Ubuntu Core is a new rendition of Ubuntu with transactional updates -"
" a minimal server image with the same libraries as today’s Ubuntu, but "
"applications are provided through a simpler mechanism. The snappy approach "
"is faster, more reliable, and lets us provide stronger security guarantees "
"for apps and users — that’s why we call them “snappy” applications."
msgstr ""
"Snappy Ubuntu Core 是 Ubuntu 的全新形态，采用事务性更新——与当前 Ubuntu "
"使用相同库的最小服务器镜像，但通过更简单的机制提供应用程序。Snappy "
"方式更快、更可靠，并允许我们为应用和用户提供更强的安全保障——这就是我们称之为「snappy」应用的原因。"

